### Demo 2: a named volume SURVIVES container deletion

$ docker volume create lab2data
lab2data
$ docker run -d --name demo-vol -v lab2data:/data ubuntu:24.04 sleep infinity
c5e2183b5e8a4933f73199f9ef56a68767b0a923e3447e85ad75b03d3a07a625
$ docker exec demo-vol sh -c "echo persistent-data > /data/note.txt && cat /data/note.txt"
persistent-data

$ docker rm -f demo-vol && docker run -d --name demo-vol -v lab2data:/data ubuntu:24.04 sleep infinity
demo-vol
df34cc335ea2592ec4cffaf44142fdd4672dbcf9df3a0e9758cfe14633f3be93
$ docker exec demo-vol cat /data/note.txt
persistent-data
--> file SURVIVED: named volume lives outside the container lifecycle

$ docker volume inspect lab2data | grep -A2 Mountpoint
        "Mountpoint": "/var/lib/docker/volumes/lab2data/_data",
        "Name": "lab2data",
        "Options": null,
